// Title: PowerShell Download Pattern
// ID: 3b6ab547-8ec2-4991-b9d2-2b06702a48d7
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), oscd.community, Jonhnathan Ribeiro
// Date: 2019-01-16
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
// Description: Detects a Powershell process that contains download commands in its command line string
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_new-object*" and process.command_line like "*_net.webclient).*" and process.command_line like "*_download*") and (process.command_line like "*_string(*" or process.command_line like "*_file(*")) and (((process.executable endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\powershell.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\pwsh.exe")) or ((process.pe.original_file_name == "PowerShell_ISE.EXE" or process.pe.original_file_name == "PowerShell.EXE" or process.pe.original_file_name == "pwsh.dll"))))
